cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "datasource-flow: IDTX Flow as a Godot extension, with USD and VRM import"
abstract: >
  A data source implements a repository, and this one reads formats that were not
  built to be queried by a game engine: USD scenes and VRM avatars, into Godot. It is
  IDTX Flow with the Godot integration built on top -- a GDExtension over godot-cpp,
  with the MToon shader and VRM addons beside it. It also supplies idtxcli, which is
  the single call transport-asset makes to fetch a content-addressed chunk.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/datasource-flow"
keywords:
  - usd
  - vrm
  - gltf
  - godot
  - gdextension
references:

  - type: software
    title: "IDTX Flow"
    authors:
      - name: "Immersive Data Center Management"
    url: "https://github.com/Immersive-Data-Center-Management/idtx-flow"
    notes: >
      The origin this is built from, credited in its own README. The undiverged mirror
      is kept separately as idtx-flow; this is the copy that carries the Godot work, so
      the two exist to keep upstream tracking and local divergence apart.

  - type: software
    title: "godot-cpp: C++ bindings for the Godot script API"
    authors:
      - name: "Godot Engine contributors"
    url: "https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp"
    notes: "Vendored at thirdparty/godot-cpp. What makes this a GDExtension rather than an engine patch."

  - type: software
    title: "Godot-MToon-Shader"
    url: "https://github.com/V-Sekai/godot-mtoon-shader"
    notes: "Vendored under addons/. MToon is what a VRM avatar expects to be shaded with."

  - type: software
    title: "Godot VRM"
    url: "https://github.com/V-Sekai/godot-vrm"
    notes: "Vendored under addons/. VRM import, which is the avatar format this fabric's clients carry."

  - type: software
    title: "OpenUSD: Universal Scene Description"
    authors:
      - name: "Pixar Animation Studios"
    url: "https://openusd.org/"
    notes: "The scene format read here, and the same one the fabric's own memory relations are stored in."
